The '''Spell of Reduction''' is a time [[Spells|spell]] that shrinks or reduces the size of an object.

==Description==
The casting seal contains a bisected [[Sigils|Sigil]], surrounded by inverted [[Signs Explained#Enlarge|Enlarge]] Signs, and 4 [[Signs Explained#Diamond|Diamond]] Signs in the gaps between. The Sigil appears to be [[Sigils Explained#Repetition|Repetition]], although it is hard to tell as it is only seen bisected. This spell works by shrinking anything within it's area of effect.

==Usage==
A Spell of Reduction is used on [[Qifrey]]'s Notebook. When the clasp is fastened, the book is pocket-sized. When the clasp is unfastened, the spell comes undone and the book returns to its original size.{{Ref|m|37|28}}

The [[Great Hall]] uses this spell to preserve and store clothes from bygone eras through [[Period Pieces]]. The casting seal is placed upon two small, wooden panels at the back of the [[contraption]]. Pulling apart these panels breaks the seal and allows the clothes to return to their original size. [[Olruggio]], [[Qifrey]] and [[Qifrey's Atelier|his aprentices]], are seen going through the contents of several of the contraptions to look for outfits to wear for [[Silver Eve]].{{Ref|m|45.5}}

Although the full seal isn't shown, [[Luluci]] uses a small piece of a cloth with what looks to be a Spell of Reduction to shrink the size of a recently returned [[Sealchair]] for convenient storage.{{Ref|m|46|6}}
